Z||000065||snafus87||09-28-2001||05:30 PM||||the U.S. No.1 on the 8th August 1976 was... Don't Go Breaking My Heart by <BR>Elton John and Kiki Dee<P>Guess that makes me 25<P>------------------<BR>JT Krupa<BR>85 GT<BR>(fastback conversion)<BR>180+ K miles<BR>Lehighton, PA||||reg||1
Z||000066||DRH||09-28-2001||05:54 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by snafus87:<BR><B>the U.S. No.1 on the 8th August 1976 was... Don't Go Breaking My Heart by <BR>Elton John and Kiki Dee<P>Guess that makes me 25<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I remember when that song came out... the summer before my senior year in high school... I guess that means my 25th reunion must be coming up soon, huh??? Well at least I don't *feel* that old (most of the time)...<P>twenty twenty two...<BR>thirty twelve...<BR>Ah heck, 42!<BR>||||reg||1
