Z||000099||Pilrulz||10-01-2001||05:53 PM||||hmmm, how do i make a long story short?  i guess i have wanted a fiero since i was about three. (no, really, i was reading car names when i was two and telling my mother how to spell them) when i was five i wanted to buy an empty hardware store building and build fieros. a man i know volunteered to sweep floors in my "fiero plant."  before i went to kindergarten, the principal did not believe that i could read, so i took a magazine article and read it.  it was an article about the cancellation of the fiero.  for a great many years i wanted a fiero, and then one showed up.  the head gasket was blown, and it smoked like the marlboro man, but the price was right: $250.  suddenly, a strange series of events began to unfold.  i now had purchased the fiero, the hardware store is emptying again, and the guy who was going to sweep my floors lost his job.  possibly a coincidence.  i will be 15 nov. 24, and have never driven my fiero, but in missouri you can get your permit, and there's not a person on this planet who can keep me from the dmv on that saturday!||||reg||12
