Z||000123||hugh||10-03-2001||07:41 AM||||I hear phrases like"older than dirt","about dinosaurs dying",let me tell you young whippersnappers it ain't easy getting old.Having to fight Indians,taking 2 days to get 20 miles on mules.You don't know how good you have it with modern appliances like telegraph,electric lights.Even paved roads!Also,Dinosaurs made nice pets if you raised them right.||||reg||7
Z||000124||Sage||10-03-2001||08:08 AM||||Hugh:<P>Don't forget having to walk to school, in 3 ft. of snow, uphill, both ways!  Having the same teacher for all your classes, in the same room no less!  Figuring out how a "hula hoop" works, and starting you car by pushing the button after you turn the key on.  Of course that was after the hand crank models, which was after the ones you started down hill, then jumped into, but it beat having to feed, water and wipe down the horses!<P>If you are indeed as old as you feel, most days I'm about 7 in my mind and 112 phiysically!<P>On maturity: "When I was a lad of 16, I couldn't believe how stupid my old man was, but I was even more amazed at how much smarter he got by the time I turned 21!"  Samuel Clemans<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||6
